{"name":"Model T","hex":"#484f49","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Model T","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The first car made by the Ford Motor Company on an assembly line. Before the Model T, cars were mostly made painstakingly by hand. The Model T helped popularize automobiling for the masses; it is widely considered the model that most did so."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Model_T"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ford Model T","blocks":[{"text":"The Ford Model T is an automobile that was produced by the Ford Motor Company from October 1, 1908, to May 26, 1927. It is generally regarded as the first mass-affordable automobile, which made car travel available to middle-class Americans. The relatively low price was partly the result of Ford's efficient fabrication, including assembly line production instead of individual handcrafting. The savings from mass production allowed the price to decline from $780 in 1910 to $290 in 1924. It was mainly designed by three engineers, Joseph A. Galamb, Eugene Farkas, and Childe Harold Wills. The Model T was colloquially known as the \"Tin Lizzie\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/1925_Ford_Model_T_touring.jpg/330px-1925_Ford_Model_T_touring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Model_T","wikidata":"Q182323"},{"title":"Model","blocks":[{"text":"A model is an informative representation of an object, person, or system. The term originally denoted the plans of a building in 16th-century English, and derived via French and Italian ultimately from Latin modulus, 'a measure'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Beta-D-Gulopyranose_Molek%C3%BClbaukasten_9288.JPG/330px-Beta-D-Gulopyranose_Molek%C3%BClbaukasten_9288.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Model","wikidata":"Q1979154"},{"title":"T","blocks":[{"text":"T is the twentieth letter of the Latin alphabet, used in the modern English alphabet, the alphabets of other western European languages and others worldwide. Its name in English is tee, plural tees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Latin_letter_T.svg/330px-Latin_letter_T.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T","wikidata":"Q9813"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg/500px-1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg/1280px-1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg/500px-1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1908 Ford Model T advertisement","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Fordsidevalve.jpg/500px-Fordsidevalve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Fordsidevalve.jpg/1280px-Fordsidevalve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Fordsidevalve.jpg/500px-Fordsidevalve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Model T engine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFordsidevalve.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/1920_Ford_Model_T_Controls_%281495288990%29.jpg/500px-1920_Ford_Model_T_Controls_%281495288990%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa